vrend: rasterization samples apart from the framebuffer's (WinBoat)

Direct3D 11.1's target-independent rasterization (ForcedSampleCount)
rasterizes with a sample count of its own, whatever the render targets have:
Direct2D renders antialiased geometry with it at feature level 11_1. GL has
it as GL_EXT_raster_multisample. A new command, VIRGL_CCMD_SET_RASTER_SAMPLES
(after the last upstream one), sets the count; the host announces it with
VIRGL_CAP_V2_RASTER_SAMPLES (bit 31: WinBoat's bits go from the top down).
Raster multisample is enabled around the guest's draws only, so the
renderer's own blits and clears don't get it.

